\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {H1 dynamics and sensitivity.} Left: the three H1 frontier restarts in support--magnitude space. Every completed restart lowers maximum defect only after increasing support above the seed value. Upper right: support as a function of accepted state index within each restart; the dashed line is the seed support. Lower right: eight nearby H1 parameter variants from the saved sensitivity probe. All eight remain pinned to the seed best objective, even though their evaluation counts differ. Together these panels show the repository's two H1 failure modes: diffusion in the actual frontier run and paralysis under more conservative settings.\relax }}{18}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:h1-dynamics}{{6}{18}{\textbf {H1 dynamics and sensitivity.} Left: the three H1 frontier restarts in support--magnitude space. Every completed restart lowers maximum defect only after increasing support above the seed value. Upper right: support as a function of accepted state index within each restart; the dashed line is the seed support. Lower right: eight nearby H1 parameter variants from the saved sensitivity probe. All eight remain pinned to the seed best objective, even though their evaluation counts differ. Together these panels show the repository's two H1 failure modes: diffusion in the actual frontier run and paralysis under more conservative settings.\relax }{figure.caption.13}{}}
